  "notes": "{支給|しきゅう} means the official provision or payment of something by an organization, government, or employer. It implies a formal, institutional context rather than casual giving.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {支給|しきゅう}する: to provide, to pay out\n- {支給|しきゅう}される: to be provided (passive, very common)\n- {支給|しきゅう}{額|がく}: amount paid\n- {支給|しきゅう}{日|び}: payment date\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {給料|きゅうりょう}を{支給|しきゅう}する: to pay a salary\n- {手当|てあて}を{支給|しきゅう}する: to provide an allowance\n- {交通費|こうつうひ}が{支給|しきゅう}される: transportation expenses are provided\n- {制服|せいふく}が{支給|しきゅう}される: uniforms are provided\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {給付|きゅうふ}: benefit payment (often government welfare or insurance)\n- {供給|きょうきゅう}: supply (broader, includes goods and services)",
